{
  "title": "57: al-Hadeed الحديد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM.\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسَبَّحَ لِلَّهِ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ (1)\nSABBAHA LELLAHE MAA FIL LSSAMAAWAATE WALAARZE WA HOWA LA’AZEEZU LHAKEEMU.\nCelebrateth the praise of God, whatever is in the heavens and the earth; and He is the Ever-Prevalent, the All-Wise\nلَهُۥ مُلْكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ يُحْىِۦ وَيُمِيتُ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (2)\nLAHUL MULKUS LSSAMAAWAATE WALAARZE LAAHUL WAYUMEETU WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nHis is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; He causeth life and causeth death; and He, over all hath power\nهُوَ ٱلْأَوَّلُ وَٱلْءَاخِرُ وَٱلظَّٰهِرُ وَٱلْبَاطِنُ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (3)\nHOWA LAAWLU WALAAKHERU WALZZAAHERU WALBAATENU WA HOWA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’ALEEMUN.\nHe is the First and the Last and the Manifest and the Hidden: and He is the Knower of all things\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ فِى سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ ٱسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى ٱلْعَرْشِ يَعْلَمُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا وَمَا يَنزِلُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيهَا وَهُوَ مَعَكُمْ أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُمْ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (4)\nHOWA LLAZEAA KHALAQAL LSSAMAAWAATE WALAARZA FIL SETTATE AAYAMIN SUMMA STAWAA A’LAL LA’ARSHE YA’LAMO MAA YALEJU FIL LAARZE WA MAA YAKHROJO MINHAA WA MAA YANZELU MENAL LSSAMAAE WA MAA YAA’RUJU FEEHAA WA HOWA MA-A’KUM AAYNA MAA KUNTUM WALLLAHU BEMAA TAA’MALOONA BASEERUN.\nHe it is who created the heavens and the earth in six periods, then firmly established (Himself) over the ‘Arsh’ (the Seat of supreme authority)’, knoweth He whatever entereth the earth, and whatever goeth forth from it, and whatever descendeth from the heaven, and whatever goeth up into it; and He is with you wherever ye be; and God, is the Seer of whatever ye do\nلَّهُۥ مُلْكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَإِلَى ٱللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ ٱلْأُمُورُ (5)\nLLAHU MULKUS LSSAMAAWAATE WALAARZE WAEELAA LAAHIR TURJA-U’L LAUMOORU.\nHis is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and unto God (alone) arc returned (all) affairs\nيُولِجُ ٱلَّيْلَ فِى ٱلنَّهَارِ وَيُولِجُ ٱلنَّهَارَ فِى ٱلَّيْلِ وَهُوَ عَلِيمٌۢ بِذَاتِ ٱلصُّدُورِ (6)\nYOOLEJU LLAYLA FIL LNNAHAARE WAYOOLEJU LNNAHAARA FIL LLAYLE WA HOWA A’ALEEMUN BE-ZAATIS LSSUDOORE.\nHe causeth the night to enter in upon the day, and causeth (He) the day to enter in upon the night, and He (alone) is the Knower of whatever is in the breasts\nءَامِنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَأَنفِقُوا۟ مِمَّا جَعَلَكُم مُّسْتَخْلَفِينَ فِيهِ فَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ مِنكُمْ وَأَنفَقُوا۟ لَهُمْ أَجْرٌ كَبِيرٌ (7)\nAAMENOOA BE-LAAHIR WARASOOLEHE WAAANFEQOOA MIMMAA JAA’ALAKUM MMUSTAKHLAFEENA FEEHE FALLAZEENA AAMANOOA MENKUM WAAANFAQOOA LAHUM AAJRUN KABEERUN.\nBelieve ye in God and His Apostle (Muhammad)! and spend ye (in charity) of whatever He hath made you the successors thereof; for whosoever among you believe and spend (in charity), for them is a recompense very great\nوَمَا لَكُمْ لَا تُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلرَّسُولُ يَدْعُوكُمْ لِتُؤْمِنُوا۟ بِرَبِّكُمْ وَقَدْ أَخَذَ مِيثَٰقَكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ (8)\nWA MAA LAKUM LAA TUMENOONA BE-LAAHIR WALRRASOOLU YADU’OOKUM LETUMENOOA BE-RABBEKUM WA QAD AAKHAZA MEESAAQAKUM EEN KUNTUM MMUMENEENA.\nAnd what reasons have ye that ye believe not in God? And the Apostle inviteth you to believe in your Lord, and hath indeed taken a covenant from you if ye are believers\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِى يُنَزِّلُ عَلَىٰ عَبْدِهِۦٓ ءَايَٰتٍۭ بَيِّنَٰتٍ لِّيُخْرِجَكُم مِّنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِكُمْ لَرَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ (9)\nHOWA LLAZEAA YUNAZZELU A’LAA A’ABDEHEAA AAYAATIN BAYNAATIN LLEEKHREJAKUM MENAL LZZULUMAATE EELAA LNNOORE WA INNA LLLAHA BEKUM LARAOOFUN RRAHEEMUN.\nHe it is Who sendeth down unto His Servant signs manifest, so that He may bring you out of the darkness (of infidelity) into the light (of faith)’, and verily God unto you is the Most Kind and the Most Merciful!\nوَمَا لَكُمْ أَلَّا تُنفِقُوا۟ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَلِلَّهِ مِيرَٰثُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ لَا يَسْتَوِى مِنكُم مَّنْ أَنفَقَ مِن قَبْلِ ٱلْفَتْحِ وَقَٰتَلَ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ أَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَنفَقُوا۟ مِنۢ بَعْدُ وَقَٰتَلُوا۟ وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ (10)\nWA MAA LAKUM AALLAA TUNFEQOOA FIL SABEELE LAAHIR WALELLAHE MEERAASU LSSAMAAWAATE WALAARZE LAA YASTAWEAA MENKUM MAN AANFAQA MEN QABLE LFATHE WAQAATALA AOOLAAAEKA AAA’ZAMU DARAJATAN MENAL LLAZEENA AANFAQOOA MEN BA’DO WAQAATALOOA WAKULLAN WA-A’DAR LLLAHU LHUSNAA WALLLAHU BEMAA TAA’MALOONA KHABEERUN.\nAnd what reasons have ye that ye spend not in the way of God, and God’s is the heritage of the heavens and the earth; alike are not among you those who spent before the victory and fought and (those who did not), they are more exalted in rank than those who spent and fought afterwards; and unto all hath promised God goodness; And verily God, of whatever ye do, is All-Aware\nمَّن ذَا ٱلَّذِى يُقْرِضُ ٱللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضَٰعِفَهُۥ لَهُۥ وَلَهُۥٓ أَجْرٌ كَرِيمٌ (11)\nMMAN ZAL LLAZEAA YUQREZUL LLLAHA QARZAN HASANAN FAYUZAAE’EFAHU LAHUL WALAHUAA AAJRUN KAREEMUN.\nWho is he who would loan unto God a goodly loan? so that He may double it for him, and for him shall be a noble recompense\nيَوْمَ تَرَى ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتِ يَسْعَىٰ نُورُهُم بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَبِأَيْمَٰنِهِم بُشْرَىٰكُمُ ٱلْيَوْمَ جَنَّٰتٌ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلْفَوْزُ ٱلْعَظِيمُ (12)\nYAWMA TARAL LMUMENEENA WALMUMENAATE YASA’AA NOORUHUM BAYNA AAYDEEHEM WABEAAYMAANEHEM BUSHRAAKUMU LYAWMA JANNAATUN TAJREAA MEN TAHTEHAL LAANHAARU KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ZAALEKA HOWA LFAWZU LA’AZEEMU.\nThe Day thou shalt see the faithful men and faithful women, with their light running before them, and on their right hand (shall be given) glad tidings for you of that Day! Gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, to abide therein; That is the great achievement\nيَوْمَ يَقُولُ ٱلْمُنَٰفِقُونَ وَٱلْمُنَٰفِقَٰتُ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ ٱنظُرُونَا نَقْتَبِسْ مِن نُّورِكُمْ قِيلَ ٱرْجِعُوا۟ وَرَآءَكُمْ فَٱلْتَمِسُوا۟ نُورًا فَضُرِبَ بَيْنَهُم بِسُورٍ لَّهُۥ بَابٌۢ بَاطِنُهُۥ فِيهِ ٱلرَّحْمَةُ وَظَٰهِرُهُۥ مِن قِبَلِهِ ٱلْعَذَابُ (13)\nYAWMA YAQOOLU LMUNAAFEQOONA WALMUNAAFEQAATU LELLAZEENA AAMANOOA NZUROONAA NAQTABES MEN NNOOREKUM QEELA RJEU’OOA WARAAAKUM FALTAMESOOA NOORAN FAZUREBA BAYNAHUM BESOORIN LLAHU BAABUN BAATENUHU FEEHE LRRAHMATU WAZAAHERUHU MEN QEBALEHE LA’AZAABU.\nOn the Day will say the hypocritical men and the hypocritical women unto those who believe: “Tarry ye for us, that we may borrow light from your light;” It shall be said: “Turn ye back and seek ye (some other) light!” So there will be set between them a wall (a harrier) with a door therein; the inside thereof shall be mercy in it, and outside it, before it shall be chastisement\nيُنَادُونَهُمْ أَلَمْ نَكُن مَّعَكُمْ قَالُوا۟ بَلَىٰ وَلَٰكِنَّكُمْ فَتَنتُمْ أَنفُسَكُمْ وَتَرَبَّصْتُمْ وَٱرْتَبْتُمْ وَغَرَّتْكُمُ ٱلْأَمَانِىُّ حَتَّىٰ جَآءَ أَمْرُ ٱللَّهِ وَغَرَّكُم بِٱللَّهِ ٱلْغَرُورُ (14)\nYUNAADOONAHUM AALAM NAKUN MMAA’AKUM QAALUD BALAA WALAAKENNAKUM FATANTUM AANFUSAKUM WATARABBASTUM WARTABTUM WAGHARRATKUMU LAAMAANEAAAU HATTAA JAAA-A AAMRU LAAHIR WAGHARRAKUM BE-LAAHIR LGHAROORU.\nThey will cry out unto them: ‘Were we not with you?’ They shall say: ‘Yea! but ye cast yourself into temptation, and ye waited (for us to be beguiled) and ye doubted (in God’s warning), and deceived you your vain desires till came the decree of God (to pass) and deceived you about God the (Arch) Deceiver\nفَٱلْيَوْمَ لَا يُؤْخَذُ مِنكُمْ فِدْيَةٌ وَلَا مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مَأْوَىٰكُمُ ٱلنَّارُ هِىَ مَوْلَىٰكُمْ وَبِئْسَ ٱلْمَصِيرُ (15)\nFALYAWMA LAA YOAKHAZO MENKUM FIDYATUN WA LAA MENAL LLAZEENA KAFARUL MAAWAAKUMU LNNAARU HEYA MAWLAAKUM WA BEASAL LMASEERU.\nSo this day shall not be accepted from you any ransom nor from those who disbelieved; your abode shall be the fire; it is your guardian, and what a wretched resort it shall be!\nأَلَمْ يَأْنِ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ أَن تَخْشَعَ قُلُوبُهُمْ لِذِكْرِ ٱللَّهِ وَمَا نَزَلَ مِنَ ٱلْحَقِّ وَلَا يَكُونُوا۟ كَٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا۟ ٱلْكِتَٰبَ مِن قَبْلُ فَطَالَ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْأَمَدُ فَقَسَتْ قُلُوبُهُمْ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَٰسِقُونَ (16)\nAALAM YAANE LELLAZEENA AAMANOOA AAN TAKHSHAA’A QULOOBUHUM LE-ELAA LAAHIR WA MAA NAZALA MENAL LHAQQE WA LAA YAKOONOOA KALLAZEENA AOOTOOA LKETAABA MEN QABLO FATAALA A’LAYHEMUL LAAMADU FA QASAT QULOOBUHUM WAKASEERUN MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nHath not the time yet come, for those who believe that their hearts become humble for the remembrance of God and what hath come down of the Truth? And (that) they should not be like unto those who were given the Book before, but (when) lengthened the ages passed over them, so it hardened their hearts; and many of them are transgressors\nٱعْلَمُوٓا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحْىِ ٱلْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا قَدْ بَيَّنَّا لَكُمُ ٱلْءَايَٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ (17)\nA’LAMOOA AANNA LLLAHA LAAHUL LAARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA QAD BAYYANNAL LAKOMUL LAAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TAA’QELOONA.\nKnow ye! that God enliveneth the earth after its death. Indeed, have We made the signs clear unto you, that ye may understand\nإِنَّ ٱلْمُصَّدِّقِينَ وَٱلْمُصَّدِّقَٰتِ وَأَقْرَضُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا يُضَٰعَفُ لَهُمْ وَلَهُمْ أَجْرٌ كَرِيمٌ (18)\nINNA LMUSSADDEQEENA WALMUSSADDEQAATE WAAAQRAZOOA LLLAHA QARZAN HASANAN YUZAAA’AFU LAHUM WA LAHUM AAJRUN KAREEMUN.\nVerily charitable men and charitable women and those who offer a goodly loan unto God, doubled shall it be unto them, and for them shall be a noble recompense\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦٓ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلصِّدِّيقُونَ وَٱلشُّهَدَآءُ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ وَنُورُهُمْ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَكَذَّبُوا۟ بَِٔايَٰتِنَآ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْجَحِيمِ (19)\nWALLAZEENA AAMANOOA BE-LAAHIR WARUSULEHEAA AOOLAAAEKA HOMUL LSSEDDEEQOONA WALSSHUHADAAU E’ENDA RABBEHIM LAHUM AAJRUHUM WANOORUHUM WALLAZEENA KAFARUL WAKAZZABOOA BEAYAATENAA AOOLAAAEKA AASHAABU LJAHEEME.\nAnd those who believe in God and His Apostle, these it is who are the truthful ones, and the witnesses with their Lord. For them shall be their recompense and their light; And those who disbelieve and belie Our signs, these are the inmates of hell\nٱعْلَمُوٓا۟ أَنَّمَا ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَا لَعِبٌ وَلَهْوٌ وَزِينَةٌ وَتَفَاخُرٌۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَتَكَاثُرٌ فِى ٱلْأَمْوَٰلِ وَٱلْأَوْلَٰدِ كَمَثَلِ غَيْثٍ أَعْجَبَ ٱلْكُفَّارَ نَبَاتُهُۥ ثُمَّ يَهِيجُ فَتَرَىٰهُ مُصْفَرًّا ثُمَّ يَكُونُ حُطَٰمًا وَفِى ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ شَدِيدٌ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرِضْوَٰنٌ وَمَا ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَآ إِلَّا مَتَٰعُ ٱلْغُرُورِ (20)\nA’LAMOOA AANNAMAA LHAYAWTU LDDUNYAA LAE’EBUN WA LAHWUNW WAZEENATUN WATAFAAKHURUN BAYNAKUM WATAKAASURUN FIL LAAMWAALE WALAAWLAADE KAMASALIL GHAYSIN AAA’JABA LKUFFAARA NABAATUHU SUMMA YAHEEJU FATARAAHU MUSFARRAL SUMMA YAKOONU HUTAAMAN WA LAAKHERATE A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN WAMAGHFERATUN MENAL LAAHIR WAREZWAANUN WA MAA LHAYAWTU LDDUNYAA EELLAA MATAAU’U LGHUROORE.\nKnow ye! That the life of this world is only a sport and play, a gaiety and a boasting and the lustful-vying in the multi-plication of wealth and children, is like unto the rain therewith springeth up the vegetation, it pleaseth the husbandmen; then it is withered away, and thou seest it becometh yellow, then becometh it stubble crumbleth down; And in the hereafter is a severe chastisement and (also) forgiveness from God, and (His) pleasures; and naught is the life of this world but means of illusion\nسَابِقُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰ مَغْفِرَةٍ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا كَعَرْضِ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ أُعِدَّتْ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦ ذَٰلِكَ فَضْلُ ٱللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَن يَشَآءُ وَٱللَّهُ ذُو ٱلْفَضْلِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ (21)\nSAABEQOOA EELAA MAGHFERATIN MMEN RABBEKUM WA JANNATIM A’ARZUHAA KAA’ARZE LSSAMAAE WALAARZE AUE’EDDAT LELLAZEENA AAMANOOA BE-LAAHIR WARUSULEHE ZAALEKA FAZLUL LAAHIR YUTEEHE MAN YASHAAA WALLLAHU ZUL LFAZLE LA’AZEEME.\nVie ye in hastening unto forgiveness from your Lord and unto a garden whose extent is like the extent of the heaven and the earth, prepared for those who believe in God and His Apostles; that is the grace of God, He bestoweth it upon whomsoever He willeth; and God is the Lord of Mighty Grace\nمَآ أَصَابَ مِن مُّصِيبَةٍ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَا فِىٓ أَنفُسِكُمْ إِلَّا فِى كِتَٰبٍ مِّن قَبْلِ أَن نَّبْرَأَهَآ إِنَّ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ يَسِيرٌ (22)\nMAA AASAABA MEN MMUSEEBATIN FIL LAARZE WA LAA FEAAAA AANFUSEKUM EELLAA FIL KETAABIN MMEN QABLE AAN NNABRAAAHAA INNA ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHIR YASEERUN.\nBefalleth not any disaster in the earth or in your own selves save it is in a Book, ere We cause it to be, verily that is easy for God\nلِّكَيْلَا تَأْسَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ مَا فَاتَكُمْ وَلَا تَفْرَحُوا۟ بِمَآ ءَاتَىٰكُمْ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخْتَالٍ فَخُورٍ (23)\nLLEKAYLAA TAASAWA A’LAA MAA FAATAKUM WA LAA TAFRAHOOA BEMAA AATAAKUM WALLLAHU LAA YOHIBBUL KULLA MUKHTAALIN FAKHOORIN.\nLest distress ye yourselves for what escapeth you, and be over- joyous for what He hath granted you; and God lovcth not an arrogant boaster\nٱلَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ وَيَأْمُرُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ بِٱلْبُخْلِ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلْغَنِىُّ ٱلْحَمِيدُ (24)\nLLAZEENA YABKHALOONA WAYAAMUROONA LNNAASA BELBUKHLE WAMAN YATAWALLA FA INNA LLLAHA HOWA LGHANEAAAU LHAMEEDU.\nThose who are niggardly and enjoin upon people niggardliness; and whosoever turneth away (from charity) then verily God is He who is Self-Sufficient, the Most Praise-Worthy\nلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا بِٱلْبَيِّنَٰتِ وَأَنزَلْنَا مَعَهُمُ ٱلْكِتَٰبَ وَٱلْمِيزَانَ لِيَقُومَ ٱلنَّاسُ بِٱلْقِسْطِ وَأَنزَلْنَا ٱلْحَدِيدَ فِيهِ بَأْسٌ شَدِيدٌ وَمَنَٰفِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَنصُرُهُۥ وَرُسُلَهُۥ بِٱلْغَيْبِ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَوِىٌّ عَزِيزٌ (25)\nLAQAD AARSALNAA RUSULANAA BELBAYNAATE WAAANZALNAA MA-A’HOMUL LKETAABA WALMEEZAANA LEEQOOMA LNNAASU BELQESTE WAAANZALNAA LHADEEDA FEEHE BAASUN SHADEEDUN WAMANAAFEU’U LIN-NAASE WALEEA’LAMA LLLAHU MAN YANSURUHU WARUSULAHU BELGHAYBE INNA LLLAHA QAWEAAAUN A’AZEEZUN.\nIndeed, sent We Our apostles with clear proofs, and sent We down with them the Book and the scale that people may establish themselves in justice; and sent We down iron wherein is latent (in its use) mighty power and also benefits for mankind and that God may prove who helpeth Him and His apostles in secret; Verily God is All-Strong the Ever-Prevalent\nوَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا وَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِى ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا ٱلنُّبُوَّةَ وَٱلْكِتَٰبَ فَمِنْهُم مُّهْتَدٍ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَٰسِقُونَ (26)\nWA LAQAD AARSALNAA NOOHAN WAEEBRAAHEEMA WA JA-A’LNAA FIL ZURREETEHEMAA LNNUBOOTA WALKETAABA FAMENHUM MMUHTADIN WAKASEERUN MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nAnd indeed sent We Noah and Abraham, and endowed We in their seed the Prophethood and the Book, so among them are some who are guided aright; and most of them are transgressors\nثُمَّ قَفَّيْنَا عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَٰرِهِم بِرُسُلِنَا وَقَفَّيْنَا بِعِيسَى ٱبْنِ مَرْيَمَ وَءَاتَيْنَٰهُ ٱلْإِنجِيلَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِى قُلُوبِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُ رَأْفَةً وَرَحْمَةً وَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ٱبْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنَٰهَا عَلَيْهِمْ إِلَّا ٱبْتِغَآءَ رِضْوَٰنِ ٱللَّهِ فَمَا رَعَوْهَا حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهَا فََٔاتَيْنَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ مِنْهُمْ أَجْرَهُمْ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَٰسِقُونَ (27)\nSUMMA QAFFAYNAA A’ALAA AASAAREHEM BERUSULENAA WA QAFFAYNAA BEE’EESAA BNE MARYAMAL WAAATAYNAAHU LEENJEELA WA JA-A’LNAA FIL QULOOBE LLAZEENA TTABAU’OOHU RAAFATAN WA RAHMATAM WARAHBAANEETAN BTADAU’OOHAA MAA KATABNAAHAA A’LAYHIM EELLAA BTEGHAAA REZWAANE LAAHIR FAMAA RAA’AWHAA HAQQA REA’AAYATEHAA FAATAYNAA LLAZEENA AAMANOOA MINHUM AAJRAHUM WAKASEERUN MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nWe made Our apostles to follow in their footsteps, and sent We after them Jesus, son of Mary, and We gave him the Evangel; and We put into the hearts of those who followed him kindness and compassion; but (as to) the monastic life, they invented it themselves. We prescribed not on them save seeking the pleasure of God, and this they observed not as they ought to have observed it; and gave We unto those of them who believed their (due) recompense; but many of them are transgressors\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ ٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَءَامِنُوا۟ بِرَسُولِهِۦ يُؤْتِكُمْ كِفْلَيْنِ مِن رَّحْمَتِهِۦ وَيَجْعَل لَّكُمْ نُورًا تَمْشُونَ بِهِۦ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ (28)\nYAAAAAYHAA LLAZEENA AAMANOOA TTAQOOA LLLAHA WAAAMENOOA BERASOOLEHE YUTEKUM KEFLAYNE MEN RRAHMATEHE WAYAJA’AL LAKUM NOORAN TAMSHOONA BEHIL WA YAGHFIR LAKUM WALLLAHU GHAFOORUN RRAHEEMUN.\nO’ ye who believe! Fear ye (the wrath of) God and believe in His Apostle; He will give you a twofold of His Mercy, He will appoint for you a light wherein ye shall walk (straight on the Right Path) and He will forgive you; and God is Oft- Forgiving, the Most Merciful\nلِّئَلَّا يَعْلَمَ أَهْلُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ أَلَّا يَقْدِرُونَ عَلَىٰ شَىْءٍ مِّن فَضْلِ ٱللَّهِ وَأَنَّ ٱلْفَضْلَ بِيَدِ ٱللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَن يَشَآءُ وَٱللَّهُ ذُو ٱلْفَضْلِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ (29)\nLLEALLAA YAA’LAMA AAHLU LKETAABE AALLAA YAQDEROONA A’LAA SHAY-IN MMEN FAZLIL LAAHIR WAAANNA LFAZLA BEEDE LAAHIR YUTEEHE MAN YASHAAA WALLLAHU ZUL LFAZLE LA’AZEEME.\nSo that may know the people of the Book that they control not aught of the grace of God, and that grace is in God’s hand, He bestoweth it upon whosoever He willeth; and God is the Lord of Mighty Grace",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 29 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the reciter of this Surah will be counted from among the staunch believers. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that whoever recites all the Surahs that start with Tasbih of Allah (s.w.t.) before going to sleep, will not die before meeting the 12th Holy Imam (a.s.) and after his death, he will have the honour of being a neighbour of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that if Surah al-Hadeed and al-Mujaadelah are recited in the compulsory prayers frequently, then the reciter will never face any punishment of Allah (s.w.t.) in this world and will not see any evil from his family. If recited by a prisoner, he will be released soon. If worn on the neck as a talisman, the wearer will not be killed in war. This Surah also makes one courageous."
